{
  "id": "forms",
  "kind": "api",
  "title": "Google Forms",
  "description": "Google Forms as the signed-in Workspace user: read and edit forms, read responses — Event registration",
  "guide": {
    "summary": "Each caller's own forms: questions by id, labeled responses, revision-checked batch edits.",
    "content": "# Google Forms usage\n\nPurpose: Event registration\n\nWorkspace delegation is configured by the deployment. Each call acts as the mapped Workspace user; no argument chooses a subject. Responses, respondent email and quiz answers are user data; no configurable sensitive-field set is declared.\n\n## Finding forms and joining answers\n\nThe Forms API cannot list or search forms. Find the file through Drive, or use\nthe id after `/forms/d/` in its edit URL. The `/forms/d/e/…` responder link is\nnot a form id. A form id is also its Drive file id.\n\nA form contains items; an item may ask one question, several grid questions,\nor no question. Responses join by `questionId`, never by `itemId`. Named\nresponse reads label answers with the current question titles in form order;\nan answer to a deleted question has no title. A response may contain several\nvalues or uploaded-file references for one question. File ids join to Drive.\n\n## Reading complete responses\n\nResponses and respondent emails can contain personal information. Filter and\naggregate in `execute_code`, returning named answers only when the task needs\nthem. `submittedAfter` is exclusive UTC: retain the newest `lastSubmittedTime`\nfor the next incremental read. Google does not promise a stable response\nsnapshot. A continuation inside a changed vendor page fails `conflict`; start\nagain or use that newest timestamp.\n\nLarge grids continue inside the same item: `questionsFrom` places the returned\nrows. `omittedQuestionIds` identifies answers left out for size; read those ids\nwith `get_response`. The structural hatch exposes quiz grading and correct\nanswers, images, and option navigation that named projections omit. Temporary\nimage access destinations remain withheld.\n\n## Editing without losing structure\n\nRead the form's current revision before editing. A stale revision refuses the\nbatch as `conflict`; re-read and rebuild the requested edit. A revision guards\nconcurrent changes and does not make a repeated write safe.\n\nCreation sets only title and Drive file name. Add descriptions or questions\nafterward. `updateItem` can replace grading, images and section navigation;\nread the full item through the hatch first and use a precise `updateMask`.\nItem locations are indexes, while response answers use question ids.\n\nPublishing, sharing, deleting forms, and watch administration are outside this\nconnection. Responses are read-only; no tool submits or deletes a response.\n\n## Conventions\n\n- **Paging:** every tool whose output declares `page` is paged: `forms_api_details`, `forms_api_read`, `forms_api_search`, `get_form`, `list_responses`. While `page.hasMore` is true, pass `page.nextCursor` back unchanged using the continuation argument its schema declares; keep the original arguments. The last page has no `nextCursor`. At execute_code's per-program call limit, return page.nextCursor and continue in the next program; don't restart.\n- **Paging:** a paged `list_*` or `search_*` read takes `limit` (default 25, at most 100) and `cursor`. While `page.hasMore` is true, pass `page.nextCursor` back unchanged as `cursor`; the last page has no `nextCursor`.\n- **Paging:** on a paged hatch read, keep the original method, path, filters, limit and fields. Pass `page.nextCursor` unchanged as the top-level `cursor`; omit raw anchors on continuations. The last page has `page.hasMore: false` and no `nextCursor`. If `page.hasMore` is true without a cursor, the data is incomplete and continuation could not be confined.\n- **Results:** `fields` narrows a read's result to the dot paths you name. `truncated` lists the dot paths a result cut for size; the ids that fetch what was cut stay in the result.\n- **Hatch:** `forms_api_search` finds this API's operations and reads no account data, `forms_api_details` shows one operation's contract, and `forms_api_read` calls a reviewed read. `forms_api_write` calls a reviewed write; the host may ask the user to confirm it. An operation without a reviewed verdict is refused. 5 operations are refused by design; use `forms_api_details` with the method and path to inspect an operation's contract and refusal.\n- **Writes:** a write is sent once and never retried. When its outcome is unknown, read the target before repeating it. Writes take no idempotency key.\n- **Errors:** codes come from the vendor's statuses and error facts, never its prose. An unknown id, or one these credentials cannot reach, fails as `connector_call_failed`; this API does not tell the two apart. `conflict` means: A revision-guarded batch update returned ABORTED or FAILED_PRECONDITION with HTTP 400 or 409..\n- **Withheld values:** a value withheld for safety reads `\"[redacted]\"`. Writes refuse whole marker values and withheld links; longer prose may mention the marker. Paths and queries refuse any containment.\n"
  },
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "get_form",
      "description": "Get one Google Form: title, description, quiz and publish state, revisionId, and its items with question ids, types, and options, paged when large. Never lists forms.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "formId": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "maxLength": 256,
            "description": "Form id from its /forms/d/<formId>/edit URL or Drive; not the /forms/d/e/ responder link.",
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$"
          },
          "cursor": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "maxLength": 16384,
            "description": "Opaque page.nextCursor from this same tool and arguments."
          },
          "fields": {
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 50,
            "description": "Dot paths to keep in the form; page and cut metadata is preserved.",
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1,
              "maxLength": 200
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "formId"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "formId": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "documentTitle": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "description": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "revisionId": {
            "type": "string"
          },
